>> title: Karahi
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: chicken, indian, tomato, ginger, curry
>> counters: Curry House
>> aka: kadai, kadhai, karai, chicken karahi, kadai chicken, karahi gosht
>> pairs-with: onion-tomato-masala, naan, kachumber
>> servings: 4
>> time: 45 min
>> step.1: toast 2 min, until they crackle
>> step.2: crush coarsely, not to a powder
>> step.3: sear 6 min over high heat
>> step.4: fry 8 min, until the skins lift and the fat comes clear
>> step.5: toss in and take it to the table

Toast @coriander seeds{1%Tbs} and @dried red chiles{3}(broken, seeds shaken out) in a dry #karahi{} ~toast{2%min}, until they crackle and smell of the pan rather than the jar.

Crush @&(~1)toasted spice{} coarsely in a #mortar{}, so the pieces are still visible in the finished dish.

Sear @bone-in chicken{2%lb}(900 g; cut small, on the bone) in @ghee{3%Tbs}(42 g) with @kosher salt{1 1/2%tsp} in the karahi over high heat ~sear{6%min}.

Fry @onion-tomato masala{1%cup}(240 g; the base recipe) and @tomatoes{3%medium}(quartered) into @&(~1)seared chicken{} ~fry{8%min}, pressing the tomatoes as they go, until the skins lift away and the fat runs clear at the edge.

Toss @fresh ginger{2%Tbs}(cut in matchsticks), @green chiles{2}(slit), @butter{1%Tbs}(14 g) and @cilantro{1/4%cup}(roughly torn) into @&(~1)karahi{} with @&(~3)crushed kadai masala{}, and carry the pan to the table — the pan is the serving dish and the dish is named after it.

Quartered tomatoes and ginger in sticks: everything here is meant to still be recognisable when it arrives.
